.TH MCP-SERVER-GOOGLEOFFICE 1 "November 2026" "mcp-server-googleoffice" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mcp-server-googleoffice \- Model Context Protocol server for Google Workspace
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mcp-server-googleoffice
[\fB\-\-transport\fR \fIstdio|streamable-http\fR] [\fB\-\-read\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-single\-user\fR] [\fB\-\-tools\fR \fISERVICE\fR...] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Exposes Gmail, Drive, Calendar, Docs, Sheets, Slides, Forms, Tasks, Contacts,
Chat, Apps Script and Programmable Search as MCP tools. The default transport
is stdio. Run with \fB\-\-help\fR for all options.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID, GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET
OAuth 2.0 client credentials (secret).
.TP
.B WORKSPACE_MCP_READ_ONLY
When true, request only read-only scopes and register only read-only tools.
.TP
.B MCP_SINGLE_USER_MODE
When 1, use any stored credentials without session mapping.
.PP
The full list is in /usr/share/mcp-server-googleoffice/server.json.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcprack (1)
